cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Replay Pack Specification (.rpk): an open format for replayable Monte-Carlo diffusion-MRI walks"
message: "If you implement, emit, or consume Replay Packs, please cite this specification."
type: standard
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-27
abstract: >
  A portable, code-free file format and replay model that stores the state of a
  Monte-Carlo random walk through a diffusion-MRI substrate so the measured signal can
  be reconstructed ("replayed") for arbitrary gradient waveforms, field strengths,
  orientations, relaxation times, surface relaxivity, and magnetization-transfer
  settings without re-running the walk. The format is independent of any compression
  scheme and supports partial ("tiered") producers, enabling interoperability across
  simulators and a shared substrate bank.
authors:
  - family-names: Fick
    given-names: Rutger H. J.
    affiliation: dmrai-lab
keywords:
  - diffusion MRI
  - Monte-Carlo simulation
  - microstructure
  - data format
  - replay
